<h1><span lang="EN-US">Activate for Scanning</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <b><i style="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal;"><span class="Path">tree context menu for Transformation &gt; <a class="glossterm" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="HotSpot20791">Activate for Scanning</a> <span class="glosstext" style="display:'none';" id="POPUP168864481">If Activate for Scanning command is enabled all new scans and captured data will pass through the activated transformation, their co-ordinates will not be in the global space.</span></span></i></b><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">If</b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Activate for Scanning</b></span></span> <span lang="EN-GB">command is enabled all new scans and captured data will pass through the activated transformation, their co-ordinates will not be in the global space. The active transformation does not affects the existing data, it is applied on new scans only.</span></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">In a document there could be maximum one active transformation and it is marked with bold characters, as shown below:</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image036.gif" width="159px" height="48px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt="">&#160;</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: To use this command scanning should be enabled in your dongle options.</p>
<p class="Use"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Use</span></b> <span lang="EN-US">this command when you need to scan in a specific co-ordinate system.</span></p>
<p>Related topic: <a href="Deactivate.htm">Deactivate</a></p>

